# Phone layout: Runs, run detail and PR panel

## What to build

Make the graph-manager web UI's run pages fit a phone (360–430 px wide) with no sideways page scroll: at a 390 × 844 viewport, `document.documentElement.scrollWidth <= window.innerWidth` on `/runs`, on a finished run (`/runs/:ws/:runId`) and on a live run. The work is almost all CSS in `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/` (`Runs.css`, `RunDetail.css`, `PrPanel.css`, `TaskGraph.css`), plus small markup additions in `RunDetail.tsx` (`TaskTable`) and `PrPanel.tsx` (the project repos table): new cell class names and `data-label` attributes, so the phone layout can label the values of a card. Below 600 px: each Runs row is a two-line card, the filter bar wraps with a full-width workspace select, the run task table (today `min-width: 600px`) becomes one card per task, the PR form row is one column, the project repos table stacks as cards, and the Start run drawer's number fields are one column. Phase cards are one column below 400 px. The task graph scrolls inside its own box. Below 900 px the live run iframe fills the height under the new 48 px Shell top bar. Desktop (900 px and wider) must look exactly as today.

Already delivered by a dependency (in the codebase now; do not re-implement):
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/media.ts` exports `NARROW = "(max-width: 899.98px)"`, `PHONE = "(max-width: 599.98px)"`, `COARSE = "(pointer: coarse)"` and `useMedia(query): boolean` (it returns `false` when `window.matchMedia` is missing, as in jsdom).
- `--app-h` is set on `<html>` to the visual viewport height in px. Use `var(--app-h, 100dvh)` wherever you need the page height.
- `ui/base.css` has `@media (pointer: coarse)` rules: 40 px hit areas on the shared buttons (`.btn`, icon buttons, segmented options, list rows) and `font-size: 16px` on `input`, `select`, `textarea`.
- Safe-area padding (`env(safe-area-inset-*)`) on `.gm-shell`, toasts, drawer and dialog footers.

This is CSS-first. In CSS, write the breakpoints as literal media queries: `@media (max-width: 599.98px)` (PHONE), `@media (max-width: 899.98px)` (NARROW), `@media (max-width: 399.98px)` for the phase cards. You do not need `useMedia` in this task unless a markup change really needs it (it should not).

Out of scope: `Shell.tsx`/`Shell.css` (the top bar and nav drawer are built by another task running in parallel), `ui/base.css`, the Terminals page, Workspaces/Projects/Reviewers/Settings/Login, `ui/Drawer.tsx`/`ui/Dialog.tsx`, and the engine's live page in `packages/graph-execution/src/web`. Do not edit those files, to avoid merge conflicts.

## Context: files to read before implementing

- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Runs.css` (whole file, 169 lines) — rows grid at lines 42–80, the existing container query for two-line rows at lines 108–124, the `@media (max-width: 900px)` block at 125–128, the Start run drawer styles at 130–169 (`.start-run-numbers` at 152 and its `@media (max-width: 480px)` at 155–157, `.start-run-providers` at 132–133).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Runs.tsx` (lines 180–235: `RunRow` markup with cells `.runs-c-status`, `.runs-c-run`, `.runs-c-type`, `.runs-c-provider`, `.runs-c-tasks`, `.runs-c-created`, `.runs-c-action`; lines 470–520: the filter bar `.runs-filters` with `.runs-ws-select`, `.runs-search`, `.runs-header-spacer`, `.runs-group-toggle`; lines 245–290: the group header rows `.runs-group`).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/RunDetail.css` (whole file, 99 lines) — `.run-detail.is-live` at line 3, live iframe at 23–33, `.run-detail-body` grid at 42–48, `.phase-cards` at 50–73 (2 columns at `max-width: 640px`, line 73), `.task-graph-card` at 75–80, task table at 82–98 (`.task-table { min-width: 600px; }` at line 83, the 6-column grid at 84–86).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/RunDetail.tsx` (lines 52–104: `TaskTable`; lines 106–123: `LiveFrame` with `.run-live-wrap` / `iframe.run-live`; lines 295–380: the run header `.run-detail-head`; lines 396–404: the live branch renders `<div className="page run-detail is-live">`).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/TaskGraph.tsx` (lines 19–20: fixed node metrics, a full graph is `nodeW 200 + colGap 60` per layer; lines 54–56: `.task-graph-scroll` > `.task-graph` with an inline pixel `width`/`height`). It is reused in compact mode by the Terminals run pane: do not change the metrics.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/TaskGraph.css` (line 2: `.task-graph-scroll { overflow-x: auto; ... }`; line 3: `.task-graph { position: relative; margin: 0 auto; }`).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/PhaseCards.tsx` (line 157: `<section className="phase-cards">`; line 159: each `.phase-card`).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/PrPanel.css` (whole file, 39 lines) — `.pr-form-row` 2-column grid at line 18, `.pr-actions` at 23, `.pr-project-repos` table at 33–39.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/PrPanel.tsx` (lines 252–275: `.pr-form-row` with Branch and Base; lines 465–512: the project table `<table className="pr-project-repos">` with `<th>Repo</th><th>{noun}</th>` and per-repo `<tr data-testid="pr-repo-<name>">` with `td.pr-project-repo` and `td.pr-project-state`).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/RunOptionsFields.tsx` (lines 109–126: the two `.start-run-numbers` grids) and `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/StartRunDrawer.tsx` (line 551: the provider `Segmented` with `className="start-run-providers"`).
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/base.css` (lines 31–34: `.page` padding, `var(--space-4)` = 16 px below 900 px; lines 166–180: `.segmented`/`.segmented-option`) — read only, do not edit.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/styles.css` (lines 58–64: legacy `.table` rules, line 64 `@media (max-width: 900px) { .table { display: block; overflow-x: auto; } }`; lines 70–74 legacy `.start-run`) — read only. No run page uses the `.table` or `.start-run` class (`grep` finds only `.table-row`, `.table-group`, `.runs-table`, `.start-run-*`), so these legacy rules do not affect this task; do not edit `styles.css`.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/ui/tokens.css` (lines 68–81): `--space-1` 4px … `--space-5` 20px, `--space-8` 48px, `--control-h` 36px, `--control-h-dense` 32px.
- `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/RunDetail.test.tsx` (lines 1–30 render helper; lines 193–219 the test "shows the phase cards, the graph and the task table of an applied run") and `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/PrPanel.test.tsx` (lines 214–245: "renders a row per repo with the open PR, the failed repo's error and Retry").
- `TESTING.md` at the repo root, section "graph-manager" (around line 126) and "graph-manager UI checklist (agent-browser)" (around line 272): how to start the fake forge and the server and log in. `apps/graph-manager/scripts/ui-smoke.sh`: a complete script that brings up the fake forge + server on free ports, clones `octo/hello`, starts a fake run (`--provider fake`) and drives agent-browser (`ab() { agent-browser --session "$SESSION" "$@"; }`). Reuse it for the browser check (`KEEP=1` keeps its temp dir).

## Patterns to follow

**CSS conventions:** tokens only (`var(--sf)`, `var(--bd)`, `var(--fg3)`, `var(--space-N)`, `var(--radius-lg)`), one rule per line in the compact style the files already use, a short comment above each new block. Put each phone block at the END of the file (or right after the rules it overrides) so it wins over the earlier rules of the same specificity. The existing narrow pattern to mirror is the Runs container query (`Runs.css:108-124`):

```css
@container (max-width: 820px) {
  .runs-head { display: none; }
  .runs-table .runs-row {
    grid-template-columns: 104px auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    grid-template-areas: "status run run action" "type provider tasks created";
    row-gap: 6px; padding-top: 10px; padding-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .runs-c-status { grid-area: status; }
  ...
}
```

**Card labels:** a value that loses its column header in a card gets a `data-label` attribute in the TSX and a phone-only `::before`:

```css
@media (max-width: 599.98px) {
  .task-table-row [data-label]::before { content: attr(data-label) " "; color: var(--fg3); font-family: var(--font-sans); }
}
```

`::before` text is not part of `textContent`, so the existing tests that compare `textContent` (e.g. `task-elapsed-01` is `"2m10s"`) keep passing.

**Test pattern:** jsdom computes no layout, so only test the markup you add. Mirror `RunDetail.test.tsx:193-219` (`renderAt(WS)`, `vi.stubGlobal("fetch", ...)`, `screen.getByTestId(...)`). Example:

```ts
expect(screen.getByTestId("task-elapsed-01").getAttribute("data-label")).toBe("Elapsed");
```

## Step-by-step tasks

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/Runs.css`

- **IMPLEMENT**: after the `@media (max-width: 900px)` block (line 128), add a `/* Phone: run rows are cards; the filter bar wraps. */` block `@media (max-width: 599.98px) { ... }`:
  - Run rows as cards (status badge and run name on line 1, the row action on the right; type, provider, task count and created time on line 2): 
    ```css
    .runs-table .runs-row {
      grid-template-columns: auto auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
      grid-template-areas: "status run run action" "type provider tasks created";
      column-gap: var(--space-2); padding: 10px var(--space-3);
    }
    .runs-c-action { min-width: 0; max-width: 45vw; }
    .runs-c-action .runs-failure { max-width: 100%; }
    .runs-progress { display: none; }  /* keep the 3/5 count, drop the bar on a phone */
    ```
    The container query already hides `.runs-head` and sets the grid areas; this block only re-sizes the columns (the `104px` status column is too wide) so line 2 fits in about 300 px. Check that the row is still a single grid (no `display` change) so `role="row"` / `role="cell"` stay as they are.
  - Filter bar: `.runs-filters { gap: var(--space-2); }`, `.runs-ws-select { flex: 1 1 100%; }`, `.runs-ws-select select { flex: 1 1 auto; max-width: none; }` (today `max-width: 260px`, line 30), `.runs-search { flex: 1 1 100%; }`, `.runs-filters .runs-header-spacer { display: none; }`.
  - Group header rows (`.runs-table .runs-group`, line 83): `gap: var(--space-2) 10px;` so the wrapped path, branch, pill and the "Open terminal" button do not overflow; `.runs-group-path { flex: 1 1 100%; }`.
  - Summary cards (line 6): `.runs-cards { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }` (three 160 px cards do not fit at 328 px).
- **IMPLEMENT** (Start run drawer, same file): change the `@media (max-width: 480px)` block at lines 155–157 to `@media (max-width: 599.98px)` so `.start-run-numbers` is one column on every phone, and add in it `.start-run-providers { flex-wrap: wrap; height: auto; }` and `.start-run-providers .segmented-option { flex: 1 1 30%; min-height: var(--control-h); border-top: 1px solid var(--bd); }` so the provider names (claude, codex, opencode, qwen, …) never get clipped in a 312 px drawer body. Keep `.start-run-providers .segmented-option` font and padding.
- **GOTCHA**: the container query (`@container`, measured on `.runs-table-wrap`) and the `@media` block both match on a phone; same specificity, so the later one in the file wins — keep the phone block after line 124. Do not touch the desktop grid at line 45.
- **GOTCHA**: on `pointer: coarse`, `ui/base.css` (dependency) gives `.btn` a 40 px minimum hit area. `.btn.runs-create-pr` sets `height: 28px` (line 75) and `.btn.runs-open-terminal` `height: 26px` (line 95); if the base rule uses `min-height`, it wins and these buttons are 40 px on touch. That is wanted: do not override it.
- **GOTCHA (iOS zoom)**: `.runs-search input` (line 35, `font: 13px …`) and `.runs-ws-select select` (line 31, `font: 500 13px …`) set their own font size with a higher specificity than a plain `input, select, textarea` rule. Open `ui/base.css` and look at the dependency's `@media (pointer: coarse)` input rule: unless it already wins over these selectors (e.g. `!important`), add to Runs.css `@media (pointer: coarse) { .runs-search input, .runs-ws-select select { font-size: 16px; } }`. iOS zooms the page when a focused field is under 16 px.
- **VALIDATE**: `npm run lint`

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/RunDetail.tsx` (`TaskTable`, lines 52–104)

- **IMPLEMENT**: give the cells stable class names and labels for the phone cards, without changing text or test ids:
  - status cell (line 73): `<span role="cell" className="task-cell-status">`.
  - name cell: unchanged (`task-cell-name`).
  - attempt cell (line 82): `className="mono task-cell-num task-cell-attempt" data-label="Attempt"`.
  - elapsed cell (line 85): `className="mono task-cell-num task-cell-elapsed" data-label="Elapsed"`.
  - lines cell (line 88): add `data-label="Lines"`.
  - deps cell (line 97): add `data-label="Depends on"`.
- **GOTCHA**: keep every `data-testid` (`task-row-*`, `task-elapsed-*`, `task-lines-*`, `task-deps-*`) and the `role` attributes. Do not render the labels as text nodes: they must come from CSS `::before`, or the tests comparing `textContent` break.
- **VALIDATE**: `npx tsc -p apps/graph-manager/tsconfig.web.json --noEmit`

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/RunDetail.css`

- **IMPLEMENT**: at the end of the file add:
  ```css
  /* Phone: one card per task (status, title, elapsed / attempt, lines, deps). */
  @media (max-width: 599.98px) {
    .run-detail-body { padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-3); gap: var(--space-4); }
    .task-table { min-width: 0; }
    .task-table-head { display: none; }
    .task-table-row {
      grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
      grid-template-areas: "status name elapsed" "attempt lines deps";
      row-gap: 4px; padding: 10px var(--space-3);
    }
    .task-cell-status { grid-area: status; }
    .task-cell-name { grid-area: name; }
    .task-cell-elapsed { grid-area: elapsed; text-align: right; }
    .task-cell-attempt { grid-area: attempt; }
    .task-cell-lines { grid-area: lines; }
    .task-cell-deps { grid-area: deps; text-align: right; min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
    .task-table-row [data-label]::before { content: attr(data-label) " "; color: var(--fg3); font-family: var(--font-sans); font-size: 11px; }
    .task-cell-elapsed[data-label]::before { content: none; }  /* "2m10s" reads fine alone next to the title */
    .run-detail-head { padding: 8px var(--space-3); gap: 8px; }
    .run-head-divider { display: none; }
    .run-id { min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
    .run-head-actions { margin-left: 0; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  }
  /* Very small phones: one phase card per row. */
  @media (max-width: 399.98px) { .phase-cards { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  ```
  Place the 399.98 px rule after line 73 (the 640 px 2-column rule) or at the end, so it wins.
- **IMPLEMENT** (live iframe): the live page is `.page.run-detail.is-live` (line 3, `height: 100%`). Below 900 px the Shell shows a 48 px top bar (`<header class="gm-topbar" data-testid="gm-topbar">`, built by a parallel task). Add:
  ```css
  /* Below 900px the live page fills the visual viewport under the 48px Shell top bar. */
  @media (max-width: 899.98px) {
    .run-detail.is-live { height: calc(var(--app-h, 100dvh) - 48px - env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px)); }
  }
  ```
  The `env(safe-area-inset-top)` term is there because `.gm-shell` is padded by it (dependency). After the Shell task lands, `.gm-main` should not scroll on a live run; if `.gm-main` already sizes itself to the space under the top bar, `height: 100%` gives the same result — check in the browser (step below) that `.gm-main` has `scrollHeight === clientHeight` and that the iframe's bottom edge is at the bottom of the viewport.
- **IMPLEMENT** (task graph card): `.task-graph-card { overflow: hidden; }` is not wanted (it would clip focus rings); instead make sure the card and `.run-detail-main` keep `min-width: 0` (they do, lines 45 and 75) so the graph's own box scrolls.
- **GOTCHA**: `.task-table-card` (line 82) keeps `overflow-x: auto` for widths 600–899 px where the 600 px table is still used.
- **VALIDATE**: `npm run lint`

### UPDATE `apps/graph-manager/src/web/pages/TaskGraph.css`

- **IMPLEMENT**: line 2 becomes `.task-graph-scroll { overflow: auto; -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch; overscroll-behavior-x: contain; max-width: 100%; padding: var(--space-2) 0; }`. Do not change the node metrics in `TaskGraph.tsx` and keep `.task-graph { margin: 0 auto; }` (centred when it is narrower than the box; when wider, the auto margin resolves to 0 and the box scrolls).
- **GOTCHA**: the compact graph in the Terminals run pane uses the same class (`.task-graph-scroll.compact`); the change must not add a vertical scrollbar there: `overflow: auto` only scrolls when content is larger, so it is fine, but look at the Terminals run pane once in the browser at desktop width.
- **VALIDATE**: `npx vitest run src/web/pages/TaskGraph.test.tsx` (from `apps/graph-manager`)

