### CHECK in a browser at 390 × 844 (agent-browser)

- Build and start the stack: `KEEP=1 bash apps/graph-manager/scripts/ui-smoke.sh` runs the whole loop (fake forge, server, clone `octo/hello`, a `--provider fake` run, Create PR) and prints the temp dir it kept; or bring it up by hand as `TESTING.md` "graph-manager" shows (`npm run build -w graph-execution && npm run build -w graph-manager`, fake forge on a free port, `GM_PASSWORD=pw … node apps/graph-manager/dist/server/main.js`, log in). Restart the server after a rebuild (it indexes static files at startup).
- `agent-browser set viewport 390 844`, log in, and on `/runs`, on the finished fake run (`/runs/github~octo~hello/<runId>`), on its `#pr` view and, if you can get one (a fake run with `{"task:3":{"attempts":[{"hang":true}]}}` in `GRAPH_EXECUTION_FAKE_SCRIPT`, see TESTING.md "Fake provider scripts"), a live run: `agent-browser eval 'document.documentElement.scrollWidth <= window.innerWidth'` must print `true`. Take a screenshot of each and LOOK at it: cards are readable, nothing is clipped, the task graph scrolls inside its card. Open the Start run drawer (`start-run` button) and check the provider row and number fields fit. Repeat at `set viewport 360 740`.
- At `set viewport 1440 900`, take screenshots of the same pages and compare with before: the desktop layout must be unchanged.
- Always clean up: kill the server/forge and the run page (pid in `.graph-execution/<run-id>/web.json`), `agent-browser close`.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] At 390 × 844 and 360 × 740, `document.documentElement.scrollWidth <= window.innerWidth` is `true` on `/runs`, a finished run page, its `#pr` view and a live run page.
- [ ] Below 600 px each Runs row is a two-line card: status badge and run id on line 1 with the action (Create PR / PR link / failure text) on the right; type, provider, task count and created time on line 2. The filter bar wraps and the workspace select is full width.
- [ ] Below 600 px the run task table has no `min-width` and shows one card per task: status, title + id, elapsed on line 1; "Attempt n", "Lines +a −d", "Depends on ← …" on line 2. The column header row is hidden.
- [ ] Phase cards: 4 columns ≥ 641 px, 2 columns to 400 px, 1 column below 400 px.
- [ ] The task graph scrolls inside `.task-graph-scroll` (`overflow: auto`, `-webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch`); the page never scrolls sideways.
- [ ] PR panel: `.pr-form-row` is one column below 600 px; the project repos table is a stack of bordered cards with "Repo" and the PR/MR label shown above each value.
- [ ] Start run drawer: `.start-run-numbers` is one column below 600 px; every provider option is fully visible.
- [ ] Below 900 px the live run iframe fills the height under the 48 px top bar (`var(--app-h)` based) and `.gm-main` does not scroll.
- [ ] At 1440 × 900 the Runs page, run detail, PR panel and Start run drawer look as before.
- [ ] `data-label` attributes and the `task-cell-status` / `task-cell-attempt` / `task-cell-elapsed` classes are present; all existing `data-testid`s and cell `textContent` are unchanged.
- [ ] Tests pass: `npx vitest run src/web/pages/RunDetail.test.tsx src/web/pages/PrPanel.test.tsx src/web/pages/Runs.test.tsx src/web/pages/TaskGraph.test.tsx src/web/pages/StartRunDrawer.test.tsx` (from `apps/graph-manager`).

## Validation commands

```bash
# Type / lint (repo root)
npm run typecheck && npm run lint

# Tests for this slice (from apps/graph-manager)
cd apps/graph-manager && npx vitest run src/web/pages/RunDetail.test.tsx src/web/pages/PrPanel.test.tsx src/web/pages/Runs.test.tsx src/web/pages/TaskGraph.test.tsx src/web/pages/StartRunDrawer.test.tsx && cd ../..

# Full suite (repo root)
npm test

# Browser check (not part of npm test): see "CHECK in a browser" above
KEEP=1 bash apps/graph-manager/scripts/ui-smoke.sh
```
